1.3.2 (14.10.26)
- improved fix for the pickup/put down error

1.3.1 (13.10.26)
- added support for new cursor API
- fixed rare errors when picking up objects (eventHandler[IE_MoveInto] failed. Lua error: Can't remove 8 of 0 items)

1.3.0 (02.10.26)
- removed 2nd positioning teleport for dropped items, this fixes on item placed interactions:
  - mwscript's `onpcdrop` (for example `Paradox Scale` from `The Popular Plague` mod)
  - lua's `onItemActive` handlers (for example OAAB's mannequins)
- persistent corpse detection: if 0.52's `isPersistent` property is available - use it
- added OAAB's mannequins to persistent corpse list
- enabled auto equip for corpses on item transfer - fixes mannequins not equipping items

1.2.0 (16.09.26) Most of these changes were released way earlier as unversioned tweaks
- fixed errors happening if controller shoulder button is pressed while inventory is not open
- distinguish left and right apparel in type column
- new API to disable all windows (requested by Quick Loot mod to facilitate activation of scripted containers)
- added setting to scale icons in grid mode
- made modified alchemy determine known effects, like in vanilla
- fixed some TR Data ingredients not displaying all their effects because they have gaps in effects
- do not send mercantile skillUsed if skillGain is 0 - same as vanilla
- scale effect, value, weight and armor class icons with text size
- fixed wrong Mercantile skill gains
- fixed merchants not selling not-equipped items that have same item record as the ones they have equipped
- show proper message when trying to sell/buy/store summoned items
- added option for tooltips to show stolen item details
- fixed no stolen indicator for items in owned containers
- added option to ignore container capacity (in Gameplay section)
- send skill use when successfully pickpocketing item
- vanilla parity: do not consider items and containers being owned it they have global variable and that variable has non 0 value

1.1.0 (6/4/26)
- Added Russian localization by Sergey Rudyi

1.0.1 (6/3/26)
- Fixed error spam when pressing category cycle buttons without a focused item

1.0.0 (6/2/26)
- Initial release